<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temple of Athena Lindia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Sanctuary of Athena Lindia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> Lindia stands on the acropolis of Lindos on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, one of the most famous sanctuaries of the Greek world. The surviving Doric temple was rebuilt in the fourth century BCE after a fire in 392 BCE, within a complex of stairs, a monumental gateway and stoas added in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a>. The Lindian Chronicle of 99 BCE recorded the gifts dedicated there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/temple-of-athena-lindia.jpg" alt="Temple of Athena Lindia" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jebulon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athena_Lindos_temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
